Fix build-ios: workload pin + Info.plist XML versions (Xcode 26.6 compatible)

Root cause: SDK 10.0.404 selected workload set 10.0.404, which installs
Microsoft.iOS.Sdk.net10.027.2 (27.2.10000). That .NET for iOS release requires
Xcode 27.2, but the macos-26 runner provides Xcode 26.6 (iOS SDK 26.5).
Workload set 10.0.401 ships .NET for iOS 26.5.10318, the release that supports
Xcode 26.6, so pin it in global.json (the CLI refuses --version when global.json
already specifies a workload version). A verification step keeps the workflow
and global.json in sync.

Separately, CompileAppManifest failed because AssetStudio.Mobile/Platforms/iOS/Info.plist
used non-numeric version strings in the XML declaration and plist root element
("v0.16.45" / "v0.16.46"). Both must be valid numeric versions ("1.0").

--- a/global.json
+++ b/global.json
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
   "sdk": {
     "version": "10.0.400",
     "rollForward": "latestPatch",
-    "allowPrerelease": false
+    "allowPrerelease": false,
+    "workloadVersion": "10.0.401"
   }
 }

--- a/.github/workflows/build-ios.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/build-ios.yml
@@ -11,6 +11,13 @@ permissions:
 jobs:
   build-ios:
     runs-on: macos-26
+    env:
+      # Keep in sync with sdk.workloadVersion in global.json. That setting pins
+      # the CLI to workload set 10.0.401 (.NET for iOS 26.5.10318, which supports
+      # the Xcode 26.6 on macos-26); newer sets require Xcode 27.x. The CLI
+      # rejects --version when global.json already specifies a workload version,
+      # so the install step relies on global.json instead.
+      IOS_WORKLOAD_SET: 10.0.401
 
     steps:
       - name: Check out source
@@ -28,5 +35,16 @@ jobs:
       - name: Install iOS workload
         run: dotnet workload install maui-ios
+
+      - name: Verify workload set
+        shell: bash
+        run: |
+          set -euo pipefail
+          workload_version="$(dotnet workload --version | tr -d '[:space:]')"
+          echo "Installed workload set: $workload_version"
+          if [[ "$workload_version" != "$IOS_WORKLOAD_SET" ]]; then
+            echo "::error::Expected workload set $IOS_WORKLOAD_SET, found '$workload_version'. Xcode 26.6 compatibility requires $IOS_WORKLOAD_SET (keep global.json in sync)."
+            exit 1
+          fi
 
       - name: Select Xcode
         run: |

--- a/AssetStudio.Mobile/Platforms/iOS/Info.plist
+++ b/AssetStudio.Mobile/Platforms/iOS/Info.plist
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-<?xml version="v0.16.45" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
 <!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
-<plist version="v0.16.46">
+<plist version="1.0">
 <dict>
